WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.147
Do not assume every view is writable.

00:00:02.147 --> 00:00:06.142
A simple one-table view may support automatic updates.

00:00:06.142 --> 00:00:11.722
A join or aggregate view does not have the same direct row mapping.

00:00:11.722 --> 00:00:15.322
Materialized views are stored query results, not ordinary write-through interfaces.

00:00:15.322 --> 00:00:20.642
Always check the actual PostgreSQL behavior for the view definition you are designing.

00:00:20.642 --> 00:00:27.192
Connect this idea to an analytics team exposing a stable reporting view to dashboard users.

00:00:27.192 --> 00:00:32.882
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:32.882 --> 00:00:38.167
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:45.057
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:45.057 --> 00:00:49.981
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
